@node Dashboards and Views
@chapter Dashboards and Views
@anchor{views}
@cindex dashboards
@cindex views

This chapter covers the read-only surfaces of beads.el: the project board
(the dashboard), the tabulated issue lists, the issue detail view, and the
eldoc previews that show issue data in any buffer.  Together they are the
day-to-day way to watch a store; the write commands live in
@ref{Issue Workflow}.  Every view command and user option is listed in
@ref{Command and Variable Reference}.

@menu
* The Board::
* List and Show Views::
* Eldoc Previews::
@end menu

@node The Board
@section The Board
@cindex project board
@cindex dashboard
@cindex vui

@deffn Command beads
Open the project board: the single front door of beads.el and the same
command as @code{beads-dashboard-status}.  Run @kbd{M-x beads}, or press
@kbd{D} from the dispatch menu (@pxref{Transients}).
@end deffn

The board is a @code{vui} buffer.  Each section is a component that loads
its own data asynchronously inside a @code{vui-error-boundary}, so one slow
or failing @command{bd} query never blocks the rest of the board.  The
@code{bd status} snapshot itself is rendered as the clickable
@strong{Stats} section (@pxref{Listing Issues} for the list views the
board links to).

If you are unsure which Beads store a buffer acts on, the header names it,
and buffer-local store scoping keeps every command pointed at the same
store (@pxref{Store Scoping}).

